error[XML001]: unescaped `<` in the text of `<script>`
 --> tests/ui/xml001-script-less-than.scx:2:29
  |
2 |   <script>for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) { }</script>
  |                             ^ `<` starts a tag here, but no element name follows it
  |
  = note: in character data `<` always starts markup; a comparison operator must be escaped or placed in a CDATA section
  = help: escape the operator as `&lt;` (and `&` as `&amp;`), or wrap the whole script body in `<![CDATA[ ... ]]>` so it needs no escaping
  = spec: XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition) §2.4 Character Data and Markup
help: escape `<` as `&lt;`
  |
2 |   <script>for (var i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) { }</script>
  |                             ~~~~

